  "prefLabel": "Pda 101.23 Mooring",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Pda 101.23 “Mooring” means a mooring anchor, or other object, structure, apparatus or stationary point, whose purpose is to provide for securing a vessel to the bottom of state tidal waters and which is designed to be left in position permanently or on a seasonal basis, including, but not limited to, floats and rafts, together with attached anchors, chains, cables, ropes, pennants and related equipment, with or without a mooring buoy.\n\nSource. #8760, eff 11-18-06 (formerly Pda 101.15)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/pda100-700.html"
